# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# People Book — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real values.
# See README.md for a walkthrough.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LLM: phrasing and capture ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Groq. Free tier, and the hackathon's "Beyond the Big Two" prize excludes
# Anthropic and OpenAI as the PRIMARY model — so keep GROQ_MODEL off Claude/GPT.
# Your own key from https://console.groq.com/keys -- the free tier is enough.
#
# Do not share one key across projects. Rotating it for one silently breaks the
# others (nothing is extracted and every reply falls back to a placeholder, which
# looks like a working chatbot), and they compete for the same rate limit, so a
# dev server running alongside this one makes both flaky.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# Optional. The reply model is separate from the extraction model on purpose:
# extraction is consequential, the reply is two or three grounded sentences and it
# was most of the wait. Leave unset to use GROQ_MODEL for both.
# GROQ_MODEL_REPLY=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# ── Account lookup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No configuration needed. A Walrus Memory account is found by reading the
# AccountRegistry, which is a permanent, append-only public Table<address, ID>
# on Sui. So the app resolves your account from your address in one read, on
# any device, with nothing stored off-chain and no indexer to run.
#
# Set these only to point at a specific deployment.
# MEMWAL_REGISTRY_ID=0x...
# MEMWAL_PACKAGE_ID=0x...

# ── Session ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HMAC key for the httpOnly cookie carrying the verified Sui address.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Walrus Memory (MemWal on Sui mainnet) ──────────────────────────────────
# The relayer's live packageId is read from its /config endpoint at runtime, so
# a package rotation does not break the app. These two are the mainnet
# AccountRegistry / fallback pair. Only MEMWAL_REGISTRY_ID is genuinely required:
# /config does not publish a registry id, and if the live package changes, the
# app tells you to update this rather than failing obscurely.
MEMWAL_SERVER_URL=https://relayer.memory.walrus.xyz
MEMWAL_REGISTRY_ID=0x8bf82c9e09e36b8d1c38298f68b7cb68e7b8762887e7592add9986d5e9cf199f
# Optional overrides, if you need to pin a specific deployment:
# MEMWAL_PACKAGE_ID=

# ── The app's own delegate key ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: npm run keygen
#
# This key is REGISTERED ON-CHAIN into each user's own MemWalAccount by that
# user, so it is scoped to them and revocable by them. It is NOT a master key:
# it cannot address a memory space it was never granted into.
MEMWAL_DELEGATE_KEY=
# MEMWAL_PRIVATE_KEY is accepted as an alias for the same 32-byte Ed25519 seed --
# it is the name the MemWal docs use. Set one or the other, not both.
# MEMWAL_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── Sui (server side: account creation, delegate registration) ─────────────
SUI_RPC_URL=https://fullnode.mainnet.sui.io:443
SUI_NETWORK=mainnet

# ── Sui (browser side — must be VITE_ prefixed to reach the client) ─────────
VITE_SUI_RPC_URL=https://fullnode.mainnet.sui.io:443
VITE_SUI_NETWORK=mainnet

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_ variables are substituted into the client bundle AT BUILD TIME. Setting
# one in the Vercel dashboard after the first deploy does nothing -- the bundle
# was already built without it. Both must be present when the deployment builds.
#
#   GROQ_API_KEY          required
#   SESSION_SECRET        required. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Regenerating it logs
#                          everyone out, which is correct and worth knowing.
#   MEMWAL_DELEGATE_KEY    required
#   MEMWAL_REGISTRY_ID     required (/config does not publish one)
#   MEMWAL_SERVER_URL      optional, has a mainnet default
#   VITE_SUI_NETWORK       build-time, required for the client
#   VITE_SUI_RPC_URL       build-time, required for the client
#
# `npm run verify:deploy <url>` checks a deployed URL for exactly these.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
